{
  "stage": 7,
  "repo": "fde-07-durable-hitl",
  "title": "Human-in-the-Loop & Durable Workflows",
  "tagline": "Agent workflows that survive crashes, wait days for a human, never refund twice, and leave a record legal can trust.",
  "why": "An agent that can issue a $900 refund needs a manager to approve it, and the approval may come hours later, after a deploy or a crash. If the process restarts and runs the refund again, that is real money. This repo shows the pattern that Temporal and similar engines use: the event history is the checkpoint, every step is replayed from it, side effects are keyed so they happen once, and every human decision is chained into an audit trail.",
  "covers": [
    "Event-sourced engine: state is a fold over history; each loop pass writes one event. A crash after any persisted event resumes to the same event sequence and final state (tested at every crash point)",
    "Tasks with retries and exponential backoff; final failure runs saga compensations in reverse",
    "Approval gates: conditional (amount over a limit), quorum, role check, separation of duties, duplicate-vote guard, timeout, one escalation",
    "Idempotency keys per workflow run (run_id or a hash of the start input): a task re-run after a crash returns its earlier result",
    "Slack Block Kit and Teams Adaptive Card approval messages; Slack request-signature check with a 5-minute replay window",
    "Hash-chained accountability trail of votes, refusals, escalations and side effects"
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "Not Temporal itself: no worker fleet, task queues or persistence layer; history is returned to the caller to store",
    "Timers are virtual (signal timestamps), not wall-clock",
    "No live Slack or Teams app: the message JSON and the signature check are real, the posting is not",
    "The crash test stops after an event is saved; the 'effect ran but its event was lost' window relies on the side-effect store honouring the idempotency key"
  ],
  "ops": [
    {
      "op": "run",
      "label": "Wait for a human",
      "help": "A $900 refund passes lookup and draft, then stops at the manager gate. status is waiting: store history and resume when someone clicks.",
      "input": {
        "workflow": {
          "id": "refund-SO-77",
          "steps": [
            {
              "name": "lookup",
              "type": "task",
              "task": "lookup_customer"
            },
            {
              "name": "draft",
              "type": "task",
              "task": "draft_refund"
            },
            {
              "name": "manager_ok",
              "type": "approval",
              "approver_roles": [
                "support_manager"
              ],
              "quorum": 1,
              "timeout_ms": 3600000,
              "escalate_to": [
                "director"
              ],
              "when_field": "refund_amount",
              "when_gt": 500
            },
            {
              "name": "issue",
              "type": "task",
              "task": "issue_refund",
              "compensate": "reverse_refund"
            },
            {
              "name": "notify",
              "type": "task",
              "task": "notify_customer"
            },
            {
              "name": "close",
              "type": "task",
              "task": "close_ticket"
            }
          ]
        },
        "input": {
          "customer_id": "C-1001",
          "order_id": "SO-77",
          "amount": 900,
          "requested_by": "agent-7"
        }
      }
    },
